# OPUS GUBERNATIO PARTICIPANT PACKAGE og-participant-2026.08-v21
#
# SUCCESSOR to og-participant-2026.08-v20, whose checksum record is preserved unchanged at
# code_audit/run52_participant_package_v20_checksums.sha256 and describes the tree as v20 left
# it. This record describes the LIVE TREE.
#
# RUNS 54 AND 55. THE FIRST LINK IN THIS CHAIN WHOSE SEQUENCE-BEARING DELTA IS A DELETION. ONE
# of the seventy files LEFT the package and FIVE of the remaining sixty-nine moved. The deletion
# is stated first because it is what a reader most needs to know, because it is sequence-bearing,
# and because it moves the SET rather than a member of it. Its authority is the owner's ruling at
# section 8 of the Run 54 order and section 6 of the Run 55 order.
#
# THE ONE SEQUENCE-BEARING EXCEPTION, NAMED, AND WHAT BECAME OF IT:
#
# assets/js/deepdive.js -- SEQUENCE-BEARING. DELETED, not edited. Every earlier exception in
#   this chain named a sequence-bearing file whose BYTES moved; this one names a sequence-bearing
#   file that is GONE. It is declared here and in server/tools/participant_packages.py as
#   V20_TO_V21_DELETED and V20_TO_V21_SEQUENCE_EXCEPTION, and SEQUENCE_BEARING_FILES is NOT
#   shortened -- SEQUENCE_BEARING_FILES_FROM_V21 is a separate five-member tuple, so every
#   historical comparison from v7 to v20 is still read against the six it was taken against, and
#   a SECOND sequence-bearing file disappearing still fails.
#
#   WHY IT WENT. The client-side deep-dive surface was reached by NO ROUTE this service serves.
#   index.html carried a comment recording that deepdive.js is not loaded there; research/
#   deepdive.html was linked from nothing; and the sole call site of LinDeepDive.render sat
#   inside the file being deleted. All 78 of its panels gated on the legacy client-side signals
#   blob at store.js:727, which a project computed through the real pipeline does not have.
#   research/deepdive.html and the @app.get("/research/deepdive.html") route in
#   server/app/main.py went with it, on the reasoning that a route still serving a deleted page
#   would be a second front door. Measured in a browser: that URL returns HTTP 404 and
#   deepdive.js appears in no document.scripts. The guarantee that no served route loads a
#   client-side model is now UNCONDITIONAL rather than confined to one route, which is the
#   stricter of the two.
#
#   NON-VACUITY, PINNED TO AN EXPLICIT COMMIT HASH. assets/js/deepdive.js existed at bf36ef6 at
#   174,212 bytes, sha256 afc1e2efa5d56acdf81551054404fa3bace5aee11e0efab94ef3be7b6708bda3 --
#   byte for byte the entry at line 81 of the v20 record above, which independently confirms
#   that the v20 record described the live tree. A proof of absence is never written against a
#   relative reference here: Run 54 wrote its own against HEAD~1 and they decayed silently into
#   false proofs that still passed as later commits walked the reference back.
#
# THE FIVE THAT MOVED, AND WHAT MOVED INSIDE EACH:
#
# assets/js/app.js -- Run 54 phase C. The project list's Manage control NAVIGATES to the project
#   detail page, and the redundant Open control is REMOVED. This REVERSES the stop Run 52 took
#   under its section 8.1, on the owner's ruling at section 9 of the Run 54 order. THE ORDER OF
#   WORK WAS NOT NEGOTIABLE AND WAS NOT NEGOTIATED: Manage was re-bound FIRST and measured in a
#   real browser reaching the detail page of its OWN row's project, per row and per surface,
#   and only THEN was Open removed, and the reachability was re-measured after the removal. No
#   project's detail page was unreachable at any point.
#
# assets/js/ingest.js -- Run 55 phase A. openInlineManage takes an optional host element. When
#   it is absent the row behaviour is what it always was; when it is supplied the panel is
#   appended there instead of to the portfolio row's <li>. THE SIX HANDLERS ARE NOT REWRITTEN.
#
# assets/js/detail.js -- Run 55 phase A. The project detail page gains a host element inside
#   .detail-head, stamped with the viewed project's id, and mounts that same panel into it. The
#   six operational controls the accordion carried -- Save info, Upload documents, Recompute
#   this project, Reset signals, Archive, Close -- are therefore ON THE DETAIL PAGE of the
#   project being viewed. Measured in a real browser on three projects: each renders exactly
#   once, the panel reads back THAT project's id and no other, and zero admin panels remain on
#   any portfolio row. Archive and Reset signals are destructive and carried NO confirmation
#   dialog before the move; they carry none after it, and their handler bodies are
#   BYTE-IDENTICAL to their pre-move bytes -- this was a move, not a rewrite.
#
# assets/css/radar.css -- Run 55 phase A. The four dead .li-open rules are removed. They styled
#   the Open control that Run 54 phase C removed and had no subject left in the DOM.
#
# index.html -- Run 54 phase B. A COMMENT that pointed at the deleted file is rewritten. NO
#   RENDERED TEXT CHANGED.
#
# NO RENDERED IDENTIFIER CHANGED and no naming sweep was run. No step of the decision sequence,
# no reveal gate, no lock, no randomization, no questionnaire, no server contract and no
# append-only record moved.
#
# NO SERVER COMPUTATION MOVED: 101 registered, 63 in service, voting exactly A1.7 and A1.8, no
# stored figure changed, and the behaviour digest is RE-DERIVED and unchanged. The v20 record is
# NOT regenerated: it describes the tree as v20 left it and stays the evidence for anything
# collected under v20.
#
